# RUNTIME LOGS AND REPORTS -- owner ruling 2026-09-05: `record()`'s output stays
# BESIDE THE MEDIA or in a local ignored directory, and MUST NEVER reach a
# repository file.
#
# MEASURED BEFORE ADDING THESE, so this is a belt and not a repair: every
# write-mode `open()` in the record() chain already targets a path outside the
# checkout --
#   merge_video_repair.py  target      = path.join(tools.tmpFolder, ...)
#   merge_plan_report.py   destination = report_path(produced_file_path)
#   main_gestionar_show.py             = join(out_folder_final, basename)+'.log.error'
# THE RULING HOLDS BY CONSTRUCTION. These patterns exist because `git check-ignore`
# said log.error, log.out, foo.mkv.log.error and merge_plan.html would ALL have been
# TRACKED if one ever landed here -- e.g. a run with tmpFolder inside the checkout.
log.error
log.out
log.log
*.log.error
*.log.out
merge_plan.html
*.merge_plan.html
